Machine learning approach for atmospheric tomography for satellite imaging

To achieve atmospheric tomography for a moving satellite against a static background starfield,
we need to simulate the atmospheric phase screens and retrieve satellite data.

This is a clean up of my last 18 months of work, with the intention of adding a robust testing regime to ensure confidence.
I have recently run into times when the results were not robust and I was never sure if it was my code or the algorithms themselves.

Data preparation
 - Phase screens
 - Satellite and starfield information
 - Model configurations

Simulation
 - Running tomography
 - Training models
 - Save results and constituent model states

Data visualisation
 - Show statistics and graphs


